# dev — web development reference lookups

## mdn — MDN Web Docs

  mdn <query>                 Search MDN, show top 5 results with summaries + URLs
  mdn <query> -o              Open top result in browser
  mdn <query> -n <count>      Show more results (default: 5)
  mdn <query> -n <count> -o   Show more results and open top in browser
  mdn "fetch api"
  mdn "css grid" -o
  mdn "web workers" -n 10
  mdn "intersection observer" -n 3 -o

## cani — caniuse.com

  cani <feature>              Open caniuse.com search in browser (default)
  cani <feature> -u           Print URL only, do not open browser (pipeable)
  cani "css grid"
  cani "webp"
  cani "container queries" -u

## goto — bookmarks

  goto <tag>                Open bookmark in browser (single match opens directly)
  goto <tag> -u             Print tag + URL only, do not open browser
  goto                      List all bookmarks (no query = always lists)

  Bookmark files:
    topics/dev/bookmarks          Committed to dotfiles (shared)
    topics/dev/bookmarks.local    Gitignored (machine/work-specific)

  Format: <tag>  <url>  <description>
  Tip: use specific tags (goto go/docs) to guarantee a single match

## Notes
  MDN uses an undocumented but stable JSON search API — returns real summaries.
  caniuse has no per-feature CLI API — browser is the only real option.
  Browser opener: 'open' (macOS) or 'xdg-open' (Linux), detected automatically.
  Flags for mdn can be combined in any order: mdn "css grid" -n 10 -o
